{"id": "EUVD-2026-98691", "enisaUuid": "c83fdef5-998e-3d48-8783-b9f369d1bd0c", "description": "Serena before 2.0.0 contains an improper link resolution vulnerability that allows attackers to access files outside the project root by committing symlinks inside a repository. Project.is_path_in_project() normalizes paths lexically without resolving symlinks, so file tools like read_file and create_text_file can read or overwrite files such as SSH keys or cloud credentials.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T14:00:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T15:29:52", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/oraios/serena/issues/2144", "https://github.com/oraios/serena/commit/6f20f9b822d85bb063008e786f808d04619dd54e", "https://github.com/oraios/serena/releases/tag/v2.0.0", "https://github.com/oraios/serena/blob/v1.7.0/src/serena/project.py", "https://github.com/oraios/serena", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/serena-before-2.0.0-symlink-following-in-file-tools-allows-access-outside-project-root"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109965", "GHSA-f7x4-jgqg-5mc6"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "af07783f-568a-35e9-84ee-cf450b9185c3", "product": {"name": "serena", "vendor": {"name": "oraios"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.0.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "70e006e5-824c-3b79-aed7-743d7e8217d6", "vendor": {"name": "oraios"}}], "isExploited": false}